{% extends 'demos/upload/demo.html.twig' %}

{% block demo_container %}
    <div class="UploadDemoShell max-w-[1140px] mx-auto mb-12">
        <twig:Browser id="demo" class="shadow-blur shadow-blur--rainbow w-full" frameClass="">
            <div
                class="UploadStage Resumable"
                data-controller="upload-chunks"
                data-action="symfony--ux-upload--upload:chunk->upload-chunks#chunk symfony--ux-upload--upload:complete->upload-chunks#complete"
            >
                <div class="UploadStage_container">
                    {% for message in app.flashes('resumable_success') %}
                        <p class="UploadStage_note" data-turbo-cache="false">{{ message }}</p>
                    {% endfor %}

                    {{ form_start(form) }}
                        <div class="UploadStage_field">
                            {{ form_widget(form) }}
                            <p class="UploadStage_outcome" data-upload-chunks-target="sent">No chunk sent yet.</p>
                            <p class="UploadStage_outcome" data-upload-chunks-target="summary" hidden></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="UploadStage_actions">
                            <button
                                type="button"
                                class="UploadStage_sample"
                                data-controller="upload-samples"
                                data-upload-samples-kind-value="large"
                                data-upload-samples-size-value="{{ 1024 * 1024 }}"
                                data-upload-samples-names-value="{{ [sample_name]|json_encode }}"
                                data-upload-samples-for-value=".Resumable input[type=file]"
                                data-action="upload-samples#fill"
                            >Generate a 1 MB archive</button>
                            <button type="submit" class="UploadStage_submit">Save</button>
                        </div>
                    {{ form_end(form) }}
                </div>
            </div>
        </twig:Browser>
    </div>

    <section class="UploadDemoStory">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="config/packages/ux_upload.yaml"
                :lineStart="20"
                :lineEnd="24"
                reversed
                sticky
            >
## Chunks per uploader

Files above `chunk_size` travel in chunks, `parallel_chunks` at a time. A failed
chunk is retried up to three times before the file is marked as failed.

The defaults are 5 MB and 3. This public server accepts 1 MB at most and keeps
no file, so this uploader cuts the archive into 16 chunks of 64 KB.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>

            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="src/Form/UploadLargeFileForm.php"
                :lineStart="27"
                :lineEnd="31"
                sticky
            >
## Nothing to add in the form

The field picks the transport from the file size: one request for a small file,
chunks for a large one. Pause and resume buttons appear on chunked transfers.

Each chunk is stored as soon as it arrives. The browser keeps a signed resume
token in IndexedDB: after a reload, select the same file, the server lists the
chunks it already holds, and only the missing ones are sent.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>

            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="assets/controllers/upload-chunks-controller.js"
                :lineStart="18"
                :lineEnd="33"
                reversed
                sticky
            >
## Listen to the field

The field emits browser events while it works: `chunk` each time the server
stores one, `complete` when it holds the whole file.

The counter under the field is this Stimulus controller, bound to both events
with `data-action`. The upload does not need it: the field shows its own
progress. See the [JavaScript API](https://github.com/symfony/ux/blob/3.x/src/Upload/doc/javascript.rst).
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>

            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="src/EventListener/SlowDemoUploadListener.php"
                :lineStart="54"
                :lineEnd="78"
                sticky
            >
## Slowed down on purpose

A server stores 16 small chunks in well under a second: too fast to pause. This
listener holds each chunk of the generated archive for 700 ms.

Two chunks wait at most, for the whole site. Your own files are never slowed
down.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
